(ns mrz.ports
  "The optical (photo -> MRZ text) seam. mrz.core never depends on this —
   only a caller that needs to go from a zone IMAGE to zone TEXT does.
   Mirrors kotoba.webrtc.session's 'host injects the concrete capability'
   split: this ns defines the contract, mrz.adapters.template-ocr is one
   (R1-experimental, classical, non-neural) implementation of it.")

(defprotocol IZoneOcr
  (read-zone [ocr line-images opts]
    "`line-images` is a seq of already-cropped, already-perspective-corrected
     MRZ line images (one per MRZ line — 2 for TD2/TD3, 3 for TD1), each a
     seq of equal-length pixel-rows (grayscale intensity, 0.0-1.0) covering
     that one line's full glyph height — this protocol takes NO
     responsibility for finding or straightening the zone in a full document
     photo (see mrz.glyph's module doc for why that's a separate, harder,
     unsolved problem here). `opts` carries implementation-specific tuning
     (a template bank, glyph count). Returns a vector of decoded line
     strings, one per input line-image, or throws ex-info on a line-image
     whose row width doesn't evenly divide into `(:glyph-count opts)`
     cells."))
